---
tracker:
  kind: linear
  # api_key may be a literal token or a $VAR_NAME reference.
  api_key: $LINEAR_API_KEY
  project_slug: my-project
  active_states:
    - Todo
    - In Progress
  terminal_states:
    - Done
    - Cancelled
    - Canceled
    - Duplicate
    - Closed

polling:
  interval_ms: 30000

workspace:
  # ~ is expanded; relative paths resolve relative to this file's directory.
  root: ~/symphony-workspaces

hooks:
  after_create: |
    git clone https://github.com/my-org/my-repo.git .
  before_run: |
    git fetch origin && git checkout main && git pull
  after_run: |
    git add -A && git diff --stat HEAD
  timeout_ms: 120000

agent:
  max_concurrent_agents: 5
  max_turns: 30
  max_retry_backoff_ms: 300000
  max_concurrent_agents_by_state:
    In Progress: 3
    Todo: 2

codex:
  command: codex app-server
  # approval_policy and thread_sandbox are Codex-defined enums.
  # Consult: codex app-server generate-json-schema --out /tmp/schema
  approval_policy: auto
  turn_timeout_ms: 3600000
  stall_timeout_ms: 300000

server:
  port: 8080
---

You are a coding agent working on issue **{{ issue.identifier }}: {{ issue.title }}**.

## Issue details

- **State**: {{ issue.state }}
- **Priority**: {{ issue.priority if issue.priority is not none else "unset" }}
- **URL**: {{ issue.url or "n/a" }}
{% if issue.labels %}
- **Labels**: {{ issue.labels | join(", ") }}
{% endif %}
{% if issue.description %}

## Description

{{ issue.description }}
{% endif %}
{% if issue.blocked_by %}

## Blockers

This issue is blocked by:
{% for b in issue.blocked_by %}
- {{ b.identifier }} ({{ b.state }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if attempt is not none %}

## Context

This is retry attempt {{ attempt }}.  Review your previous work and continue
from where you left off.
{% endif %}

## Instructions

1. Read the issue description and understand what needs to be done.
2. Implement the changes required to resolve the issue.
3. Write or update tests to cover your changes.
4. Ensure the build and tests pass before finishing.
5. Commit your work with a clear message referencing {{ issue.identifier }}.
